# CMB Polarisation Power Spectra catalogue --- Planck 2018 PR3 binned
# TE and EE plus low-ell unbinned BB. Tables from Planck Legacy Archive
# (COM_PowerSpect_CMB-TE-binned_R3.02.txt,
#  COM_PowerSpect_CMB-EE-binned_R3.02.txt,
#  COM_PowerSpect_CMB-low-ell-BB-full_R3.01.txt),
# canonical paper Planck 2018 V (Aghanim et al. 2020, A&A 641:A5,
# doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201936386, arXiv:1907.12875).
#
# Each line below is one MPR row data block (NDJSON).
# Lines starting with "#" or empty lines are skipped by the
# literature_curated adapter.
#
# Single row_type "multipole_bin" catalogue. Coverage:
#   - TE binned: 19 representative bands spanning ell ~ 48 to ell ~ 1988,
#     covering the canonical alternating-sign acoustic pattern (TE crosses
#     zero ~ 5 times across the Planck range; positive lobe peaks at
#     ell ~ 315 with D_ell ~ 119 muK^2; negative lobe trough at
#     ell ~ 705 with D_ell ~ -99 muK^2).
#   - EE binned: 16 representative bands spanning ell ~ 48 to ell ~ 1988.
#     EE is always positive; peaks at ell ~ 405 (first peak, ~21 muK^2),
#     ell ~ 705 (second peak, ~38 muK^2), ell ~ 1005 (third peak, ~42 muK^2).
#   - BB unbinned low-ell: 10 representative ells from ell=2..29, all
#     consistent with noise floor (~0.01 muK^2 amplitude, fluctuating
#     around zero; no detected primordial B-modes).
#
# Headline canonical values:
#   - TE first acoustic peak: ell = 314.975, D_ell = 119.4 +/- 2.5 muK^2
#   - EE first acoustic peak: ell = 404.870, D_ell = 21.16 +/- 0.36 muK^2
#   - BB upper limit at ell=2: D_ell = -0.10 +/- 0.09 muK^2 (consistent with 0)
#
# precision_flag = "high" for all rows --- values from PLA tables verbatim
# (no rounding beyond NDJSON precision).

